      "content": "One major concern with CBAM is the risk of trade diversion, where companies may shift production to non-regulated regions to avoid the carbon levy. Another downside is the administrative complexity; tracking embedded emissions accurately across complex global supply chains is technically difficult for many businesses. Additionally, there is the risk of potential over- or under-estimation of emissions, creating uncertainty in compliance for trading partners. Finally, smaller economies or developing nations may argue that the mechanism acts as a protectionist barrier rather than a purely environmental tool.",
      "source": "target",
